:name: ZB-02 heap layout probe — observe the real allocator (sub_1411c) and pool structure
:description: Boots the real Aqara feeder firmware and inspects the inline-header free-list heap that the segmented-reassembly buffer is allocated from: reads the two pool heads ([0x2000456c] small, [0x200059cc] large) + selector flag [0x20004568], dumps the pool region, and calls sub_1411c directly a few times to reveal block headers (16-bit: 15-bit size + bit15 in-use) and where blocks land relative to each other. This establishes what is ADJACENT to the reassembly buffer that the OOB write (sub_14D08) can corrupt.

$bin=@scripts/silabs-vuln/zb02_aqara.elf
include @scripts/silabs-vuln/boot_mg21.resc

emulation RunFor "0.3"
pause
echo ">>> post-boot PC:"
cpu PC

echo ">>> heap selector flag [0x20004568]:"
sysbus ReadByte 0x20004568
echo ">>> small-pool head ptr [0x2000456c]:"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000456c
echo ">>> large-pool head ptr [0x200059cc]:"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x200059cc
echo ">>> reassembly ctx [0x20004608..0x20004614] (ctx[4]=num_seg, ctx[8]=alloc base):"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x20004608
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000460C
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x20004610
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x20004614

# --- Call the allocator sub_1411c(size) directly to see block layout ---
# alloc #1: 120 bytes (= 2 segments * 60, the reassembly-buffer size for num_seg=2)
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 13 0x2000FF00
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 14 0x00009001
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 0  120
sysbus.cpu PC 0x1411c
cpu AddHook 0x9000 "self.ErrorLog('ALLOC1 returned r0 = 0x{0:X}'.format(self.GetRegister(0).RawValue))"
sysbus.cpu Step 200
echo ">>> ALLOC1 (size 120) returned ptr:"
cpu GetRegister 0

# alloc #2: another 120 bytes to see the NEXT block placement + header of the gap
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 13 0x2000FF00
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 14 0x00009001
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 0  120
sysbus.cpu PC 0x1411c
sysbus.cpu Step 200
echo ">>> ALLOC2 (size 120) returned ptr:"
cpu GetRegister 0

quit
